<title>VIETNAM: Vietnam robusta coffee exports seen up.</title>
<headline>Vietnam robusta coffee exports seen up.</headline>
<dateline>HO CHI MINH CITY, Vietnam 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vietnam's robusta coffee exports in the 1996/97 (October/January) harvest season will reach more than 240,000 tonnes from the previous season's 231,000 tonnes, a senior official said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Doan Trieu Nhan, vice-chairman of the Vinacafe state trading corporation, told Reuters exports in the 1997/98 season should reach 250,000 tonnes. Virtually all of Vietnam's coffee production is exported.</p>
<p>&quot;Exports will be more than 240,000 tonnes,&quot; he said. &quot;It maybe 250,000 tonnes next season.&quot;  </p>
<p>Vietnam is the second biggest producer of coffee in Asia after Indonesia.</p>
</text>
